{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828289-clan-vs-covenant","id":828289,"title":"Clan vs Covenant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-11T10:31:43-08:00","id":828289,"title":"Clan vs Covenant","content":"Hi everyone<br /> <br /> Quick question. Which would take priority or have more power over a kindred his/her clan(Ventrue, daeva etc...) or their covenant (Invictus, circle of crone etc.). As i'm curious about what sort of power struggle their would be between the clans and covenants to manipulate their flock and which would have more pull.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11109-nemesis","name":"Nemesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T10:42:17-08:00","id":828291,"title":"","content":"Depends on the individual, but generally speaking, Covenant. Your Clan is the family you're born to (or rather, died to), while your Covenant is the family you choose. As in real life, different people will value those differently, but generally speaking the fact that you have no choice in the former tends to lead people to value the latter a bit more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-11-2016, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T10:58:37-08:00","id":828305,"title":"","content":"Though osnt underestimate how Clan can be valuable. It isn't like it is in Masuerade, it's not because they have these highly specific weird cultures, but rather because these people who share your Blood uniquely understand your brand of fucked up in a way the other Clans can't. Plus, your Sire is probably the person who has given you the most time, help and explanation, and may be connected to their own sire's other childer because of their shared relationship and so on.<br /> <br /> Covenants provide ideology and a lot of a Requiem's activities, so I definitely agree that for most Kindred it will be more important, just don't completely devalue how your Clan situated you in your Requiem","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T11:52:06-08:00","id":828333,"title":"","content":"<b>Covenant</b> is your large-scale priority. It concerns ideologies, moral or ethical beliefs, political alliances, and social offices among the Kindred. It encompasses ambitions and allegiances. It's zoomed out wide.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b> is your small-scale priority. It concerns families, feuds, grudges, personal loyalties, approaches to the night-to-night Requiem. It encompasses love, hate and need. It's zoomed in close.<br /> <br /> Neither of these consistently trumps the other; that's the dilemma of personal drama when they conflict. Do you side with your friends or your career? Your personal interests or the needs of the society? Your lover or your God?<br /> <br /> Sometimes one, sometimes the other. Betting on which is when is the danger of the Danse Macabre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T12:00:51-08:00","id":828339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828289-clan-vs-covenant?p=828305#post828305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though osnt underestimate how Clan can be valuable. It isn't like it is in Masuerade, it's not because they have these highly specific weird cultures, but rather because these people who share your Blood uniquely understand your brand of fucked up in a way the other Clans can't. Plus, your Sire is probably the person who has given you the most time, help and explanation, and may be connected to their own sire's other childer because of their shared relationship and so on.<br /> <br /> Covenants provide ideology and a lot of a Requiem's activities, so I definitely agree that for most Kindred it will be more important, just don't completely devalue how your Clan situated you in your Requiem</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, for sure. Clan is still important, just like family is important. Even people who hate their birth families often still make an effort to maintain a (mostly) non-hostile relationship with them, because like it or not, your family knows you intimately, as you do them. Those kinds of bonds are powerful, and birth families usually offer support structures that other ties cannot. In my games at least, the same is true of Clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T12:52:45-08:00","id":828364,"title":"","content":"I would put much greater emphasis on Covenant, personally. Clan is what you're born into, shaping you with stereotypes and those around you, but that doesn't have nearly the same gravity as the ideology you have chosen to spend the rest of immortality dedicated to. <br /> <br /> The difference between a Gangrel and a Daeva is minute compared to the difference between a member of the Invictus and one of the Carthian Movement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:08:58-08:00","id":828376,"title":"","content":"This also varies by domain, as there are some who put way more stock in a character's lineage than his political leanings, but that's more defined than just Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:37:43-08:00","id":828408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828289-clan-vs-covenant?p=828376#post828376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This also varies by domain, as there are some who put way more stock in a character's lineage than his political leanings, but that's more defined than just Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course; if the domain is in a storied European city and everyone can trace their lineages back six or aeven generations into grand families of the undead, then that's entirely different from some young punk who just knows that he and his sire were both Mekhet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T21:54:11-08:00","id":828604,"title":"","content":"Yeah, although it's worth noting that if you care about those types of lineage you also probably put more weight on Clan identity as a thing in general, since if you're clanmates you're (probably) related in some way. Of course you care more about your sire and your grandsire, but just meeting, say, a Ventrue is a leg up in an otherwise equal environment.<br /> <br /> It's in these types of environments that Clan Priscus' and Whips make some sort of sense. Otherwise they aren't really positions I understand or like much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 02-12-2016, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T04:41:57-08:00","id":828723,"title":"","content":"The following is mostly my thoughts and analysis of the game - YMMV depending on what you prefer for your table.<br /> <br /> In general, Requiem is founded on the notion that Covenant is more important than what family you were born to. Now, make no mistake, family is very important. And your sire and fellow broodmates are very likely to be highly influential when it comes to your new vampire mindset, so chances are you'll come to see things, if not exactly the same, at least closely enough that you'll at least be allied covenants (though love can turn to hate and rejection). Clan is both your vampire &quot;genetics&quot; and your nuture during that transitional period where you adapt to unlife. It informs where you come from, how you were raised, what you were taught. Its always going to be an influence on your existance. <br /> <br /> But covenant is your choice of life. You were raised to make all the decisions, and you've been released into the world to make those decisions. Your nature and nurture give you a set of parameters you're likely to operate in, but how you act in those parameters is entirely up to you. You've &quot;grown up&quot; as a vampire and are ready to make whatever you will of your Requiem. And you do that through your covenant. <br /> <br /> Clan is your past, your history. Its what you learn from so you avoid the mistakes. Covenant is your future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T11:06:38-08:00","id":828873,"title":"","content":"The five clan books show a wide variety of views on clan and its importance among vampires. They focus on five vampires from the primary clans who have been tasked with finding the history of their clan by a mysterious agent. Some of the depictions range from very tightly-knit and organized clans to it being not a consideration at all, basically as much as you might upon finding a human who was also born on Earth.<br /> <br /> Everyone seems to have gotten it right, usually covenant is more important but in some places where a single clan dominates it can be important, some cities have never had more than one clan and members who travel elsewhere may see it as more important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T20:40:07-08:00","id":830012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828289-clan-vs-covenant?p=828604#post828604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, although it's worth noting that if you care about those types of lineage you also probably put more weight on Clan identity as a thing in general, since if you're clanmates you're (probably) related in some way. Of course you care more about your sire and your grandsire, but just meeting, say, a Ventrue is a leg up in an otherwise equal environment.<br /> <br /> It's in these types of environments that Clan Priscus' and Whips make some sort of sense. Otherwise they aren't really positions I understand or like much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that blood and smoke seems to postulate or at least most of a given clan in a given city are related. Priscus may no longer make sense.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps reworked as dynastics status within a family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}